WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:09.950
In this lesson, you will learn to check whether a list contains something and use it to make decisions, like a password checker or an inventory.

2
00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:15.990
The block “list contains thing?” is true if the thing is anywhere in the list.

3
00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.910
It works in if blocks just like other conditions.

4
00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:25.340
Many games keep an inventory: a list of things the player has collected.

5
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:29.300
Add an item when collected; check the list to open a door.

6
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:32.100
Store allowed passwords in a list.

7
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:36.480
Ask for the password and check if the list contains the answer.

8
00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:44.150
Use “not” to check the opposite: if not (bag contains key) → say “You need a key!”.

9
00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:47.640
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

10
00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:51.760
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
